<article class="env-remark" id="8581FF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8581FF">Remark <span data-tag="8581FF">6.5.2.2</span>.</a> In the case where the topos $\mathfrak X$ of sheaves of sets on $\calC $ has enough points, there is a simpler description of the class $(W)$ of local equivalences: a map $F \rightarrow G$ of simplicial presheaves is a local equivalence if and only if it induces weak homotopy equivalences $F_{x} \rightarrow G_{x}$ of simplicial sets, after passing to the stalk at any point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$. We refer the reader to <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/jardine">jardine</a>]</span> for details. </p>
</article>